<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southold, New York</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Southold is a town on the North Fork of Long Island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suffolk">Suffolk</a> County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Founded in 1640 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puritans">Puritans</a> from New Haven led by the minister John Youngs, it belonged to the New Haven Colony and passed to New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a> after the English conquest of New Netherland in 1664. It is one of the oldest English towns in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southold-new-york.jpg" alt="Southold, New York" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kosboot · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Southold_Free_Library_facade_(view_from_Main_Street).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
